		(comp
			(ref "L1")
			(value "1.5uH")
			(footprint "AQROOT_Beta:Coilcraft_XFL4020")
			(description "Inductor")
			(fields
				(field
					(name "Note") "Coilcraft doc 745-1 rev 03/10/26: 1.5 uH +/-20%; DCR 14.40 mOhm typ / 15.80 max; SRF 59 MHz typ; Isat 4.1 A (10% drop) / 4.4 A (20%) / 4.6 A (30%); Irms 6.7 A (20K rise) / 9.1 A (40K). Body 4.0 x 4.0 mm +/-0.3, height 2.10 mm max, terminals 0.82 x 1.57 mm. LCSC C3033018. Coilcraft marks the start (short) lead - connect high dv/dt there for lowest EMI, and the footprint carries that orientation marker. **FBV2-S2-001: THE 'FOOTPRINT STILL BLOCKED' NOTE THAT USED TO SIT HERE IS STALE AND IS WITHDRAWN.** The land pattern was subsequently built from Coilcraft document 745-3 rev 03/10/26 'Recommended Land Pattern' with the dimensions read off the drawing leader lines rather than inferred from text order: pad 0.98 mm wide x 3.4 mm long at 2.37 mm centre-to-centre. **HEADROOM CHECK, FBV2-S2-001:** at the TPS63020 worst case - 2 A out of 3.3 V from a 3.0 V cell - the average inductor current is about 2.44 A and the peak about 2.9 A, against Isat 4.1 A at the 10 % inductance-drop point. That is 1.4x on Isat and 2.7x on Irms: adequate, and the tightest magnetics margin on the board. Measure the inductor current at first article before raising any published rail limit.")
				(field
					(name "Package") "XFL4020 shielded moulded power inductor, 4.0 x 4.0 x 2.1 mm max - LOCKED. Footprint BLOCKED: needs the official Coilcraft XFL4020 recommended land pattern; no stock KiCad XFL footprint exists.")
				(field
