				(value "Land pattern VERIFIED_VENDOR_EXACT against the C&K / Littelfuse PTS645 series datasheet (Revised VL 01/29/26), RECOMMENDED PCB LAYOUT / PCB LAYOUT panels. The drawing gives 9.5 outer-edge to outer-edge and 6.4 inner-edge to inner-edge in X, and 5.8 outer to 3.2 inner in Y, which yields pads 1.55 (X) x 1.30 (Y) on centres of +/-3.975 (X) and +/-2.25 (Y). KiCad Button_Switch_SMD:SW_SPST_PTS645Sx43SMTR92 implements 1.55 x 1.30 at (+/-3.98, +/-2.25) - exact on pad size and on the Y centre, with a 0.005 mm rounding on the X centre that is far inside any fabrication tolerance. The same land pattern is published for both the 4.3 mm SMT G Type and the 7.3 mm straight SMT variants, which is why the footprint can be locked before the actuator-height suffix is. Four physical pads; C&K numbers them 1 and 2 on the top row and 3 and 4 on the bottom row with 1-2 tied and 3-4 tied, so the KiCad footprint maps its pad 1 to the top pair and pad 2 to the bottom pair, matching the 2-pin Switch:SW_Push symbol.")
