		(comp
			(ref "U9")
			(value "ST25R3916-AQET")
			(footprint "AQROOT_Beta:ST25R3916_AQET")
			(datasheet "https://www.st.com/en/nfc/st25r3916.html")
			(description "ST25R3916 high performance NFC universal device and EMVCo reader, UFQFPN-32")
			(fields
				(field
					(name "Note") "FBV2-S2-001: **DNP -> FIT**. `U9` AND ITS ENTIRE SUPPLY-DECOUPLING NETWORK ARRIVED FROM BETA-DM MARKED DNP, WHICH DIRECTLY CONTRADICTS TWO STANDING CTO DECISIONS: D-035, 'NFC is mandatory in the FIRST Full Beta v2 fabrication. No DNP showcase shortcut', and D-055, 'NFC must be FITTED and functional on the first fabrication'. The board would otherwise have been built with a complete, fitted 13.56 MHz matching network, crystal, antenna connector and SPI wiring - and no NFC chip. FITTED WITH IT: C19 and C55 on NFC_SUPPLY, C45/C46 on VDD_D, C47/C48 on VDD_A, C49/C50 on VDD_RF, C51/C52 on VDD_AM and C53/C54 on AGDC - twelve parts that are all mandatory supply decoupling in DS12484, not options. Part is ST25R3916-AQET, LCSC C5267441 (D-126). Six pins remain deliberately unconnected - CSO, EXT_LM, AAT_A, AAT_B, CSI and MCU_CLK - because capacitive sensing, external load modulation, antenna auto-tuning and the MCU clock output are all optional features this product does not use; each carries a recorded ERC exclusion.")
				(field
					(name "Note2") "SOURCING 2026-08-23 (FBV2-S2-002) (B-71). ST25R3916-AQET is LCSC C5267441 with STOCK 6 against a need of 5 - one spare, and this is a UFQFPN-32 5x5 with an exposed pad, i.e. the single part on this board that genuinely cannot be hand-placed. Buy spares from a broadline distributor and consign. LCSC/JLC library state verified live on 2026-08-23 through the JLCPCB parts API (D-096). Stock is a snapshot, not a guarantee.")
				(field
					(name "Manufacturer") "STMicroelectronics")
				(field
					(name "MPN") "ST25R3916-AQET")
				(field
					(name "LCSC") "C5267441")
				(field
					(name "Package") "UFQFPN32 5x5x0.55, 0.5 mm pitch, 32 lands + exposed pad 33. LOCKED 2026-08-23 (FBV2-S1-004B): ST25R3916-AQET, NOT the B variant. Normal internal RF-regulator mode: VDD_IO on +3V3; VDD and VDD_TX both on NFC_SUPPLY, which is +3V3 on the first build through the R106 FIT link with the R107 DNP link as the no-respin 5 V fallback; I2C_EN grounded to select SPI; VDD_DR sourced from the VDD_RF regulated node - NOT tied to VDD_TX, which would be the regulator-bypass configuration and is not used. Regulator outputs VDD_D, VDD_A, VDD_RF and VDD_AM plus reference AGDC each carry ST-specified local decoupling. Exposed pad grounded per ST. FIRMWARE MUST SET sup3V. AAT_A/AAT_B, CSI/CSO, EXT_LM and MCU_CLK are explicit no-connects. RF front end and 27.12 MHz crystal are captured; every matching value is TUNE until STSW-ST25R004 is run.")
				(field
					(name "Footprint") "AQROOT_Beta:ST25R3916_AQET")
				(field
					(name "Datasheet") "https://www.st.com/en/nfc/st25r3916.html")
				(field
					(name "Description") "ST25R3916 high performance NFC universal device and EMVCo reader, UFQFPN-32")
			)
			(libsource
				(lib "AQROOT_Beta")
				(part "ST25R3916-AQET")
				(description "ST25R3916 high performance NFC universal device and EMVCo reader, UFQFPN-32")
			)
			(property
				(name "Note")
				(value "FBV2-S2-001: **DNP -> FIT**. `U9` AND ITS ENTIRE SUPPLY-DECOUPLING NETWORK ARRIVED FROM BETA-DM MARKED DNP, WHICH DIRECTLY CONTRADICTS TWO STANDING CTO DECISIONS: D-035, 'NFC is mandatory in the FIRST Full Beta v2 fabrication. No DNP showcase shortcut', and D-055, 'NFC must be FITTED and functional on the first fabrication'. The board would otherwise have been built with a complete, fitted 13.56 MHz matching network, crystal, antenna connector and SPI wiring - and no NFC chip. FITTED WITH IT: C19 and C55 on NFC_SUPPLY, C45/C46 on VDD_D, C47/C48 on VDD_A, C49/C50 on VDD_RF, C51/C52 on VDD_AM and C53/C54 on AGDC - twelve parts that are all mandatory supply decoupling in DS12484, not options. Part is ST25R3916-AQET, LCSC C5267441 (D-126). Six pins remain deliberately unconnected - CSO, EXT_LM, AAT_A, AAT_B, CSI and MCU_CLK - because capacitive sensing, external load modulation, antenna auto-tuning and the MCU clock output are all optional features this product does not use; each carries a recorded ERC exclusion.")
			)
			(property
				(name "Note2")
				(value "SOURCING 2026-08-23 (FBV2-S2-002) (B-71). ST25R3916-AQET is LCSC C5267441 with STOCK 6 against a need of 5 - one spare, and this is a UFQFPN-32 5x5 with an exposed pad, i.e. the single part on this board that genuinely cannot be hand-placed. Buy spares from a broadline distributor and consign. LCSC/JLC library state verified live on 2026-08-23 through the JLCPCB parts API (D-096). Stock is a snapshot, not a guarantee.")
			)
