		(comp
			(ref "MK1")
			(value "DMM-4026-B-I2S")
			(footprint "AQROOT_Beta:PUI_DMM-4026-B-I2S_4.0x3.0mm")
			(datasheet "https://api.puiaudio.com/filename/DMM-4026-B-I2S-R.pdf")
			(description "PUI Audio bottom-port MEMS I2S microphone, 7-pad, 4.0 x 3.0 x 1.0 mm")
			(fields
				(field
					(name "Note2") "SOURCING 2026-08-23 (FBV2-S2-002) (B-71). PUI Audio DMM-4026-B-I2S-R is in the LCSC catalogue as C3171792 but STOCK IS 0. Buy from Digi-Key/Mouser and consign - a 7-pad bottom-port MEMS microphone is not a hand-placement candidate. B-63 CLOSED at the same time: see the footprint file, which now carries the acoustic port, the paste pullback and the keepout. LCSC/JLC library state verified live on 2026-08-23 through the JLCPCB parts API (D-096). Stock is a snapshot, not a guarantee.")
				(field
					(name "LCSC") "C3171792")
				(field
					(name "Manufacturer") "PUI Audio")
				(field
					(name "MPN") "DMM-4026-B-I2S-R")
				(field
					(name "Package") "PUI 7-pad SMD, 4.00 x 3.00 x 1.00 mm, bottom acoustic port")
				(field
					(name "Note") "REPLACES THE OBSOLETE ICS-43434 (FBV2-S1-006). Not a pin-compatible swap: the DMM-4026-B-I2S-R has SEVEN pads and a different land pattern, so both the symbol and the footprint are new. Verified against the PUI Audio data sheet Rev A, 5/26/2021. Pin 1 LR to GND selects the LEFT I2S slot. Pin 2 CONFIG has no ICS-43434 equivalent and MUST be tied to GND - the data sheet says Pull to ground, the state of this pin is used at power-up. Pin 3 VDD 1.62 to 3.63 V with C8 100 nF local. Pin 4 GND is the ring pad around the acoustic port. Pin 7 SD tri-states off-slot, and the data sheet requires a 100 kOhm pull-down on the SD trace - that is R120. CLOCK CONSTRAINT: normal mode needs BCLK between 2.048 and 4.096 MHz, so a 16 kHz / 64-BCLK frame (1.024 MHz) would NOT keep this microphone in normal mode. Run the shared I2S bus at 48 kHz with a 64-BCLK frame - 3.072 MHz, the data sheet typical - and decimate to 16 kHz in firmware. Below 320 kHz the part drops to sleep mode at 5 uA. Startup 20 ms. Supply current 820 to 1000 uA. BOTTOM PORT: acoustic port 0.25 mm diameter in the can; the PCB needs a 1.05 mm hole concentric with pad 4, and the enclosure tunnel must align to it.")
				(field
					(name "Footprint") "AQROOT_Beta:PUI_DMM-4026-B-I2S_4.0x3.0mm")
				(field
					(name "Datasheet") "https://api.puiaudio.com/filename/DMM-4026-B-I2S-R.pdf")
				(field
					(name "Description") "PUI Audio bottom-port MEMS I2S microphone, 7-pad, 4.0 x 3.0 x 1.0 mm")
			)
			(libsource
				(lib "AQROOT_Beta")
				(part "DMM-4026-B-I2S")
				(description "PUI Audio bottom-port MEMS I2S microphone, 7-pad, 4.0 x 3.0 x 1.0 mm")
			)
			(property
				(name "Note2")
				(value "SOURCING 2026-08-23 (FBV2-S2-002) (B-71). PUI Audio DMM-4026-B-I2S-R is in the LCSC catalogue as C3171792 but STOCK IS 0. Buy from Digi-Key/Mouser and consign - a 7-pad bottom-port MEMS microphone is not a hand-placement candidate. B-63 CLOSED at the same time: see the footprint file, which now carries the acoustic port, the paste pullback and the keepout. LCSC/JLC library state verified live on 2026-08-23 through the JLCPCB parts API (D-096). Stock is a snapshot, not a guarantee.")
			)
