		(comp
			(ref "U5")
			(value "MAX98357A")
			(footprint "Package_DFN_QFN:TQFN-16-1EP_3x3mm_P0.5mm_EP1.23x1.23mm")
			(datasheet "https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/MAX98357A-MAX98357B.pdf")
			(description "Mono DAC with amplifier, I2S, PCM, TDM, 32-bit, 96khz, 3.2W, TQFP-16")
			(fields
				(field
					(name "Note2") "B-03 FOOTPRINT VERIFIED TIER 1 2026-08-23 (FBV2-S2-002). Both cited Maxim documents were retrieved and read. Package outline 21-0136 gives 16L TQFN 3x3, e = 0.50 BSC, b = 0.20/0.25/0.30, L = 0.30/0.40/0.50, and lists EXPOSED PAD VARIATIONS in which T1633-5 is 1.50/1.60/1.70 while T1633-2/-4/-7C are 0.95/1.10/1.25. THAT LOOKED LIKE A CONTRADICTION with a 1.23 mm land and it is not: Maxim land pattern 90-0032 Rev E, titled \"PACKAGE LAND PATTERN, [T1633] 16L TQFN, 3X3 MM\", is issued for PKG CODES [T1633-5], [T1633-5C] AND [T1633-7C] together and specifies ONE land for all three - EP 1.23 x 1.23, perimeter pads 0.80 x 0.30, pitch 0.50, pad centreline span 2.85, IPC-7351A, tolerance +/-0.02. So the land question does not depend on which EP variant the MAX98357AETE+T carries. Numerical comparison with Package_DFN_QFN:TQFN-16-1EP_3x3mm_P0.5mm_EP1.23x1.23mm: EP 1.23 x 1.23 EXACT; pitch 0.50 EXACT; pad INNER edge 1.025 EXACT (so EP-to-signal clearance is Maxim s own 0.410 mm); pad centre 1.4375 vs 1.425 (+0.0125, inside the drawing tolerance); pad length 0.825 vs 0.80 (+0.025 toe); pad WIDTH 0.25 vs 0.30 (-0.05, zero side fillet, but a 0.25 mm pad gap and a safer mask dam at 0.5 mm pitch). NO PROJECT-LOCAL FOOTPRINT IS NEEDED - the two deviations are <= 0.05 mm, IPC-7351B compliant, and both are on the safe side for a first build. EP paste is four 0.5 x 0.5 apertures = 66% coverage, which is correct QFN practice.")
				(field
					(name "LCSC") "C910544")
				(field
					(name "Manufacturer") "Analog Devices (Maxim)")
				(field
					(name "MPN") "MAX98357AETE+T")
				(field
					(name "Package") "TQFN-16, 3 x 3 mm, 0.5 mm pitch, exposed pad")
				(field
					(name "Note") "RETAINED after a lifecycle check in FBV2-S1-006: analog.com lists the MAX98357A as PRODUCTION with a 1ku price, so there is no sourcing reason to move. Orderable MPN MAX98357AETE+T, 16-pin TQFN, -40 to +85 C, tape and reel. Supply 2.5 to 5.5 V, so 3.3 V is in range. GAIN_SLOT CHANGED FROM GND (12 dB) TO VDD (6 dB) in FBV2-S1-006: gain is referenced to a 2.1 dBV full-scale DAC output, so at 12 dB a 0 dBFS sample asks for 5.07 Vrms while the 3.3 V rail can only deliver 2.33 Vrms - everything above about -6.8 dBFS would clip. At 6 dB, 0 dBFS maps to 2.54 Vrms, essentially the rail, so the whole digital range is usable and the output noise floor is lower. Maximum output is rail-limited either way at about 0.68 W into 8 ohm. SD_MODE is a multi-level input: above the B2 trip point (1.4 V typ) selects LEFT, below B0 (0.16 V typ) is shutdown, so a plain push-pull 3.3 V drive gives exactly the two states this design needs. R15 100 k to GND on sheet 08 holds it in shutdown at reset and boot. No series resistor is needed on SD_MODE because VDD and VDDIO are the same +3V3 net, so the data sheet VDD < VDDIO case cannot occur. Quiescent 2.4 mA at 3.7 V, standby 340 uA with BCLK stopped, shutdown 0.6 uA. Turn-on 7 ms. Speaker current limit 2.8 A. Spread-spectrum modulation around 330 kHz. FIRMWARE RULE: do NOT remove LRCLK while BCLK is present - the data sheet warns this can produce a large DC output voltage, which would burn an 8 ohm voice coil. LRCLK must be one of 8, 16, 32, 44.1, 48, 88.2 or 96 kHz.")
				(field
					(name "Footprint") "Package_DFN_QFN:TQFN-16-1EP_3x3mm_P0.5mm_EP1.23x1.23mm")
				(field
					(name "Datasheet") "https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/MAX98357A-MAX98357B.pdf")
				(field
					(name "Description") "Mono DAC with amplifier, I2S, PCM, TDM, 32-bit, 96khz, 3.2W, TQFP-16")
			)
			(libsource
				(lib "Audio")
				(part "MAX98357A")
				(description "Mono DAC with amplifier, I2S, PCM, TDM, 32-bit, 96khz, 3.2W, TQFP-16")
			)
			(property
				(name "Note2")
				(value "B-03 FOOTPRINT VERIFIED TIER 1 2026-08-23 (FBV2-S2-002). Both cited Maxim documents were retrieved and read. Package outline 21-0136 gives 16L TQFN 3x3, e = 0.50 BSC, b = 0.20/0.25/0.30, L = 0.30/0.40/0.50, and lists EXPOSED PAD VARIATIONS in which T1633-5 is 1.50/1.60/1.70 while T1633-2/-4/-7C are 0.95/1.10/1.25. THAT LOOKED LIKE A CONTRADICTION with a 1.23 mm land and it is not: Maxim land pattern 90-0032 Rev E, titled \"PACKAGE LAND PATTERN, [T1633] 16L TQFN, 3X3 MM\", is issued for PKG CODES [T1633-5], [T1633-5C] AND [T1633-7C] together and specifies ONE land for all three - EP 1.23 x 1.23, perimeter pads 0.80 x 0.30, pitch 0.50, pad centreline span 2.85, IPC-7351A, tolerance +/-0.02. So the land question does not depend on which EP variant the MAX98357AETE+T carries. Numerical comparison with Package_DFN_QFN:TQFN-16-1EP_3x3mm_P0.5mm_EP1.23x1.23mm: EP 1.23 x 1.23 EXACT; pitch 0.50 EXACT; pad INNER edge 1.025 EXACT (so EP-to-signal clearance is Maxim s own 0.410 mm); pad centre 1.4375 vs 1.425 (+0.0125, inside the drawing tolerance); pad length 0.825 vs 0.80 (+0.025 toe); pad WIDTH 0.25 vs 0.30 (-0.05, zero side fillet, but a 0.25 mm pad gap and a safer mask dam at 0.5 mm pitch). NO PROJECT-LOCAL FOOTPRINT IS NEEDED - the two deviations are <= 0.05 mm, IPC-7351B compliant, and both are on the safe side for a first build. EP paste is four 0.5 x 0.5 apertures = 66% coverage, which is correct QFN practice.")
			)
