			(property
				(name "Note")
				(value "RETAINED after a lifecycle check in FBV2-S1-006: analog.com lists the MAX98357A as PRODUCTION with a 1ku price, so there is no sourcing reason to move. Orderable MPN MAX98357AETE+T, 16-pin TQFN, -40 to +85 C, tape and reel. Supply 2.5 to 5.5 V, so 3.3 V is in range. GAIN_SLOT CHANGED FROM GND (12 dB) TO VDD (6 dB) in FBV2-S1-006: gain is referenced to a 2.1 dBV full-scale DAC output, so at 12 dB a 0 dBFS sample asks for 5.07 Vrms while the 3.3 V rail can only deliver 2.33 Vrms - everything above about -6.8 dBFS would clip. At 6 dB, 0 dBFS maps to 2.54 Vrms, essentially the rail, so the whole digital range is usable and the output noise floor is lower. Maximum output is rail-limited either way at about 0.68 W into 8 ohm. SD_MODE is a multi-level input: above the B2 trip point (1.4 V typ) selects LEFT, below B0 (0.16 V typ) is shutdown, so a plain push-pull 3.3 V drive gives exactly the two states this design needs. R15 100 k to GND on sheet 08 holds it in shutdown at reset and boot. No series resistor is needed on SD_MODE because VDD and VDDIO are the same +3V3 net, so the data sheet VDD < VDDIO case cannot occur. Quiescent 2.4 mA at 3.7 V, standby 340 uA with BCLK stopped, shutdown 0.6 uA. Turn-on 7 ms. Speaker current limit 2.8 A. Spread-spectrum modulation around 330 kHz. FIRMWARE RULE: do NOT remove LRCLK while BCLK is present - the data sheet warns this can produce a large DC output voltage, which would burn an 8 ohm voice coil. LRCLK must be one of 8, 16, 32, 44.1, 48, 88.2 or 96 kHz.")
