		(comp
			(ref "D1")
			(value "TSAL6100")
			(footprint "LED_THT:LED_D5.0mm")
			(datasheet "https://www.vishay.com/docs/81009/tsal6100.pdf")
			(description "High-power 940 nm IR emitting diode, T-1 3/4")
			(fields
				(field
					(name "LCSC") "C111836")
				(field
					(name "Sim.Pins") "1=K 2=A")
				(field
					(name "Manufacturer") "Vishay")
				(field
					(name "MPN") "TSAL6100")
				(field
					(name "Package") "T-1 3/4 leaded, 5 mm diameter, 2.54 mm lead pitch")
				(field
					(name "Note") "IR EMITTER LOCKED TSAL6100 in FBV2-S1-007, replacing the inherited TSAL6200. Verified against Vishay document 81009 Rev 1.8. 940 nm GaAlAs MQW, T-1 3/4 leaded, 5 mm diameter. Ie 170 mW/sr typ (80 min) at IF = 100 mA, ANGLE OF HALF INTENSITY plus/minus 10 degrees, radiant power 40 mW, tr/tf 15 ns. VF 1.35 V typ / 1.6 V max at 100 mA. THE BINDING LIMIT FOR 38 kHz REMOTE USE IS IFM = 200 mA, the REPETITIVE peak rating at tp/T = 0.5 with tp = 100 us. IFSM = 1.5 A is a SINGLE-PULSE surge for t <= 5 us and MUST NOT be used to justify repetitive carrier current. Continuous IF is 100 mA, PV 160 mW, RthJA 230 K/W, Tj 100 C. Selected first-build peak is 150 mA, 75 percent of IFM; worst case across rail, VF and resistor tolerance is 170 mA, still 15 percent below IFM. Average LED power over an NEC frame is about 25 mW against a 160 mW limit, so Tj rises about 6 K. TSAL6200 IS A DROP-IN FALLBACK: identical T-1 3/4 package and footprint, identical VF 1.35/1.6 at 100 mA and identical IFM 200 mA, so R24 needs no change. It trades Ie 170 -> 72 mW/sr for a beam of plus/minus 17 instead of plus/minus 10 degrees. Fit it if first-article testing shows the TSAL6100 cone is too narrow to aim comfortably.")
				(field
					(name "Footprint") "LED_THT:LED_D5.0mm")
				(field
					(name "Datasheet") "https://www.vishay.com/docs/81009/tsal6100.pdf")
				(field
					(name "Description") "High-power 940 nm IR emitting diode, T-1 3/4")
			)
