			(fields
				(field
					(name "Note") "IR LED CURRENT TRIM, DNP. No-respin provision under D-049. Fitting it in parallel with R24 raises the LED peak current without removing the fitted part: 12R alone 150 mA, 12R || 220R 158 mA, 12R || 100R 168 mA, 12R || 68R 176 mA, 12R || 47R 188 mA. NEVER LET THE PARALLEL COMBINATION FALL BELOW 10 OHM - that exceeds the 200 mA IFM repetitive rating of the TSAL6100 and TSAL6200. It is the obvious first move if the TSAL6200 fallback is fitted, since its Ie is 72 mW/sr against 170.")
