		(comp
			(ref "D13")
			(value "MHPA3528RGBCT")
			(footprint "AQROOT_Beta:MEIHUA_MHPA3528RGBCT_PLCC4_3.5x2.8mm")
			(datasheet "https://www.lcsc.com/product-detail/C409779.html")
			(fields
				(field
					(name "Manufacturer") "MEIHUA")
				(field
					(name "MPN") "MHPA3528RGBCT")
				(field
					(name "LCSC") "C409779")
				(field
					(name "Note") "FRONT RGB STATUS LIGHT, FBV2-S1-008. MEIHUA MHPA3528RGBCT, LCSC C409779, COMMON ANODE, SMD3528-4P 3.5 x 2.8 x 1.85 mm, top view, water-clear, 120 deg. PIN 1 = ANODE, 2 = BLUE K, 3 = GREEN K, 4 = RED K - this is NOT the order used by Device:LED_ARGB (2 = red, 4 = blue), so that stock symbol would have swapped red and blue. Driven directly by three PCAL9535A outputs on U2 port 0; the nets are ACTIVE LOW because the anode is the common terminal. SAFE STATE IS PROVEN, NOT ASSUMED: at power-up every PCAL pin is a high-impedance input (Configuration 06h/07h = FFh) AND the internal pull-up/pull-down is DISABLED (46h/47h = 00h), so the only current available to the LED is the data-sheet IIH/IIL leakage limit of 1 uA - roughly 1/1500 of the operating current and about 0.05 mcd, far below the threshold of visibility. When firmware then makes the pin an output it drives HIGH first, because Output port 02h/03h = FFh, so the LED stays dark through the transition and NO external pull-up is needed on any cathode node. ESD: the GREEN and BLUE dice are rated only 150 V HBM against 2000 V for RED - treat as an ESD-sensitive part in assembly and rework. Mechanically this is a single front indicator behind a diffuser; see MECHANICAL_INTERFACE_SPEC.md.")
				(field
					(name "Footprint") "AQROOT_Beta:MEIHUA_MHPA3528RGBCT_PLCC4_3.5x2.8mm")
				(field
					(name "Datasheet") "https://www.lcsc.com/product-detail/C409779.html")
				(field
					(name "Description")
				)
			)
			(libsource
				(lib "AQROOT_Beta")
				(part "MHPA3528RGBCT")
				(description "RGB LED, COMMON ANODE, SMD3528-4P PLCC-4 3.5x2.8x1.85 mm, top view, water-clear lens, 120 deg")
			)
