				(field
					(name "Note") "RED channel current-set resistor, FBV2-S1-008. R = (3.30 - VF - VOL) / IF with VF ~ 1.75 V read off the data-sheet Fig. 4 forward-current curve AT THE OPERATING CURRENT, not the 20 mA table value, and VOL ~ 0.05 V (the PCAL9535A guarantees <= 0.25 V at 8 mA, so 0.05 V is conservative at 1.5 mA). 1.500 mA nominal; 1.70 mA at the high corner (3.366 V rail, VF 1.65) and 1.18 mA at the low corner (3.234 V rail, VF 1.95, VOL 0.10). Red gets the LEAST current of the three because it is by far the most efficient - 1070 mcd typ at 20 mA against 500 mcd for blue.")
				(field
					(name "Footprint") "Resistor_SMD:R_0603_1608Metric")
				(field
					(name "Datasheet")
