				(field
					(name "Note_Sourcing") "SOURCING D-615 LIVE_RECORD. JLCPCB record read 2026-09-05T00:59:59Z: base library, stock 2802834, land 0603, Operating Temperature -55℃~+155℃; Power(Watts) 100mW; Resistance 680Ω; Temperature Coefficient ±100ppm/℃; Tolerance ±1%; Type Thick Film Resistor; Voltage-Supply(Max) 75V. Gates: land working voltage vs the highest node; 2x operating and survives single fault.")
				(field
					(name "Tolerance") "1%")
				(field
					(name "Power") "0.1W")
				(field
					(name "Note") "GREEN channel current-set resistor, FBV2-S1-008. The tabulated VF of 2.7 to 3.3 V is quoted AT 20 mA and would leave almost no headroom on a 3.3 V rail; the data-sheet Fig. 4 curve gives VF ~ 2.55 V at about 1 mA, which is what this value is derived from. 1.03 mA nominal, 1.32 mA high corner, 0.57 mA low corner. Green is the brightest die per mA (1685 mcd typ at 20 mA) so it is deliberately run the leanest. The 2.4:1 corner spread is inherent to driving a 2.55 V die from 3.3 V with only ~0.7 V across the resistor; perceived brightness goes roughly as the cube root of current, so it is a small visible change behind a diffuser.")
				(field
					(name "Footprint") "Resistor_SMD:R_0603_1608Metric")
				(field
					(name "Datasheet")
				)
				(field
					(name "Description")
