					(name "Note_Sourcing") "SOURCING D-615 LIVE_RECORD. JLCPCB record read 2026-09-05T00:59:59Z: base library, stock 456712, land 0603, Operating Temperature -55℃~+155℃; Power(Watts) 100mW; Resistance 390Ω; Temperature Coefficient ±100ppm/℃; Tolerance ±1%; Type Thick Film Resistor; Voltage-Supply(Max) 75V. Gates: land working voltage vs the highest node; 2x operating and survives single fault.")
				(field
					(name "Tolerance") "1%")
				(field
					(name "Power") "0.1W")
				(field
					(name "Note") "BLUE channel current-set resistor, FBV2-S1-008. VF ~ 2.60 V at ~1.7 mA from the data-sheet Fig. 4 curve (the 2.7 to 3.4 V table figure is at 20 mA). 1.67 mA nominal, 2.17 mA high corner, 0.86 mA low corner. Blue gets the MOST current of the three because it is the dimmest die - 500 mcd typ at 20 mA against 1685 for green - which brings the three channels to roughly 80 / 87 / 42 mcd and gives a usable white through a diffuser. This is indicator balance, not colorimetry.")
				(field
					(name "Footprint") "Resistor_SMD:R_0603_1608Metric")
				(field
					(name "Datasheet")
				)
