		(comp
			(ref "U2")
			(value "PCAL9535APW")
			(footprint "Package_SO:TSSOP-24_4.4x7.8mm_P0.65mm")
			(datasheet "https://www.nxp.com/docs/en/data-sheet/PCAL9535A.pdf")
			(description "Low-voltage 16-bit I2C-bus I/O port with interrupt and Agile I/O, TSSOP-24")
			(fields
				(field
					(name "Note2") "SOURCING 2026-08-23 (FBV2-S2-002) (B-71) - FIRST-BUILD BLOCKER. NXP PCAL9535APW,118 is LCSC C2669683 with STOCK 1 against a need of FIFTEEN (three per board, five boards). This part cannot be JLC-turnkey-sourced today. Buy fifteen plus spares from a broadline distributor and CONSIGN them to JLC so they stay MACHINE-PLACED - a TSSOP-24 at 0.65 mm pitch, fifteen times, is not a hand-assembly job. LCSC/JLC library state verified live on 2026-08-23 through the JLCPCB parts API (D-096). Stock is a snapshot, not a guarantee.")
				(field
					(name "LCSC") "C2669683")
				(field
					(name "Manufacturer") "NXP Semiconductors")
				(field
					(name "MPN") "PCAL9535APW,118")
				(field
					(name "I2C_Address") "0x20")
				(field
					(name "Note") "FBV2-S1-008: TCA9535PWR -> NXP PCAL9535APW,118. PIN-TO-PIN IDENTICAL - NXP data sheet Rev. 2, 23-Jan-2015 calls the part a pin-to-pin replacement for the PCA9535 and the TSSOP24 pinning matches the inherited symbol exactly, so no wire moved. Address 0 1 0 0 A2 A1 A0. THE SWAP IS NOT COSMETIC, and it is what makes this sheet work: (1) programmable 100 k pull-up/pull-down per bit (46h/47h enable, 48h/49h select) so RESERVED and unused pins need no external resistors, which the TCA9535 cannot do; (2) an interrupt MASK (4Ah/4Bh) and a read-only interrupt STATUS register (4Ch/4Dh) that names the changed input, where the TCA9535 forces firmware to read every port of both devices and still cannot tell which bit moved; (3) all interrupts MASKED at power-up, so bring-up is free of spurious INT; (4) four output drive strengths (40h-43h) to slow edges for EMI. POWER-UP REGISTER STATE THAT THE SAFE-STATE ANALYSIS DEPENDS ON: Configuration 06h/07h = FFh (all pins high-impedance INPUTS); Output port 02h/03h = FFh, so a pin DRIVES HIGH the instant firmware makes it an output; pull-up/pull-down enable 46h/47h = 00h, so the internal resistors are OFF and the only current at a high-Z pin is the 1 uA IIH/IIL leakage limit. FIRMWARE CONTRACT: write the Output port register BEFORE the Configuration register, or the five active-low resets and AMP_SD_MODE will glitch to their inactive state on the write that makes them outputs. Outputs sink 25 mA each for direct LED drive; abs max 50 mA per I/O, 200 mA ISS, 200 mW Ptot. Standby 1.0 uA typ at 3.3 V.")
				(field
					(name "Footprint") "Package_SO:TSSOP-24_4.4x7.8mm_P0.65mm")
				(field
					(name "Datasheet") "https://www.nxp.com/docs/en/data-sheet/PCAL9535A.pdf")
				(field
					(name "Description") "Low-voltage 16-bit I2C-bus I/O port with interrupt and Agile I/O, TSSOP-24")
			)
