			(description "Qwiic / STEMMA QT I2C connector, JST SM04B-SRSS-TB(LF)(SN), SH series 1.0 mm pitch, 4 circuit, SIDE ENTRY, surface mount, body 6.0 x 4.25 mm, 1.0 A, 50 V AC/DC, -25 to +85 C, contact resistance 20 mOhm initial. ADDED AT FBV2-EXP-002 (D-238). PIN ORDER IS THE ECOSYSTEM STANDARD, NOT A CHOICE: 1 GND (black), 2 3.3 V (red), 3 SDA (blue), 4 SCL (yellow) - identical for SparkFun Qwiic and Adafruit STEMMA QT, so every cable in either ecosystem mates it. IT ADDS NO COMPONENT: it lands on the PROTECTED EXTERNAL segment at EXT_SDA / EXT_SCL, downstream of U16 TCA4307 and of the R47/R48 22 ohm series pair and at D2's TPD4E1B06 clamp, so it inherits the hot-swap buffer, the R49/R50 1.5 k pull-ups, the series resistance and the ESD array. POWER IS ACC_3V3_SW AND THAT IS ARCHITECTURAL, NOT A PREFERENCE: U16's own VCC is already ACC_3V3_SW and the pull-ups pull to it, so feeding the port from unswitched +3V3 would create a powered-device / unpowered-bus state and invite back-feeding through the accessory's ESD diodes. ACC_5V_SW IS NEVER EXPOSED HERE.")
			(fields
				(field
					(name "LCSC") "C160404")
				(field
					(name "Manufacturer") "JST")
				(field
					(name "MPN") "SM04B-SRSS-TB(LF)(SN)")
				(field
					(name "Note_Sourcing") "SOURCING D-615 LIVE_RECORD, SUPERSEDING THE D-614 REFERENCE_RULING. The MPN was grafted at D-614 from D-238 and SOURCING_LEDGER; the LCSC code was the half DEVICE_SPEC s.16 item 8 still listed as OPEN. JLCPCB record read 2026-09-05: JST SM04B-SRSS-TB(LF)(SN), LCSC C160404, stock 69510, SH series, pitch 1 mm, 4P 1x4P, 1 A, 50 V, -25..+85 C, UL94V-0, surface mount right angle, board footprint 6 mm x 4.32 mm -- every field corroborates D-238 and the land Connector_JST:JST_SH_SM04B-SRSS-TB_1x04-1MP_P1.00mm_Horizontal. The bare order code SM04B-SRSS-TB resolves only to ZERO-STOCK JLCPCB Assembly entries, which is why the plating-suffixed string is the one D-096 requires.")
				(field
					(name "Footprint") "Connector_JST:JST_SH_SM04B-SRSS-TB_1x04-1MP_P1.00mm_Horizontal")
				(field
					(name "Datasheet") "https://www.jst-mfg.com/product/pdf/eng/eSH.pdf")
				(field
					(name "Description") "Qwiic / STEMMA QT I2C connector, JST SM04B-SRSS-TB(LF)(SN), SH series 1.0 mm pitch, 4 circuit, SIDE ENTRY, surface mount, body 6.0 x 4.25 mm, 1.0 A, 50 V AC/DC, -25 to +85 C, contact resistance 20 mOhm initial. ADDED AT FBV2-EXP-002 (D-238). PIN ORDER IS THE ECOSYSTEM STANDARD, NOT A CHOICE: 1 GND (black), 2 3.3 V (red), 3 SDA (blue), 4 SCL (yellow) - identical for SparkFun Qwiic and Adafruit STEMMA QT, so every cable in either ecosystem mates it. IT ADDS NO COMPONENT: it lands on the PROTECTED EXTERNAL segment at EXT_SDA / EXT_SCL, downstream of U16 TCA4307 and of the R47/R48 22 ohm series pair and at D2's TPD4E1B06 clamp, so it inherits the hot-swap buffer, the R49/R50 1.5 k pull-ups, the series resistance and the ESD array. POWER IS ACC_3V3_SW AND THAT IS ARCHITECTURAL, NOT A PREFERENCE: U16's own VCC is already ACC_3V3_SW and the pull-ups pull to it, so feeding the port from unswitched +3V3 would create a powered-device / unpowered-bus state and invite back-feeding through the accessory's ESD diodes. ACC_5V_SW IS NEVER EXPOSED HERE.")
			)
