		(comp
			(ref "Q10")
			(value "2N7002")
			(footprint "Package_TO_SOT_SMD:SOT-23")
			(description "N-channel MOSFET, 60 V, 115 mA, SOT-23, WAKE isolation pass gate")
			(fields
				(field
					(name "LCSC") "C8545")
				(field
					(name "Manufacturer") "onsemi")
				(field
					(name "MPN") "2N7002")
				(field
					(name "Note") "WAKE ISOLATION PASS GATE - D-091, CLOSES B-08. 2N7002 N-channel MOSFET between the exposed WAKE contact and the internal `WAKE_INT_N` line, gate driven by ACC_3V3_SW. ORIENTATION IS LOAD-BEARING: the SOURCE faces the CONNECTOR and the DRAIN faces the internal line, so the body diode's anode is on the accessory side. With ACC_3V3_SW off the gate sits at 0 V, the channel is off, and an accessory pulling the contact to ground reverse-biases the body diode against the internal 3.3 V - SO A SHORTED OR HOSTILE ACCESSORY CANNOT HOLD WAKE_INT_N LOW AND CANNOT STARVE THE INTERNAL BUTTONS. Reverse the FET and the body diode alone would defeat the whole arrangement. With ACC_3V3_SW on, `R63` holds the source near 3.3 V so VGS is 0 and the FET idles off; when the accessory pulls the contact low, VGS rises to about 3.3 V, the FET turns on and the internal line follows - the standard bidirectional pass-gate. RESIDUAL, BOUNDED AND RECORDED: if a hostile accessory DRIVES the contact to 5 V while the rail is off, the body diode conducts from source to drain and injects (5 - 3.3 - 0.7)/330 = about 3 mA into WAKE_INT_N through `R66`. That is inside every clamp on the net and is the reason `R66` is 330 Ohm rather than 100 Ohm. CONSEQUENCE (B-36): accessory-initiated wake from sleep requires ACC_3V3_SW to remain enabled during sleep, which costs the TPS22950C quiescent current plus whatever the accessory draws.")
				(field
					(name "Footprint") "Package_TO_SOT_SMD:SOT-23")
				(field
					(name "Datasheet")
				)
				(field
					(name "Description") "N-channel MOSFET, 60 V, 115 mA, SOT-23, WAKE isolation pass gate")
			)
			(libsource
				(lib "Transistor_FET")
				(part "Q_NMOS_GSD")
				(description "N-MOSFET transistor, gate/source/drain")
			)
