				(value "0.1W")
			)
			(property
				(name "Note")
				(value "TCA4307 READY pull-up, FBV2-S1-009. READY is an OPEN-DRAIN flag that is high only when EN is high AND the IN and OUT sides have actually been connected, so it is the single best bring-up observable on this sheet: it distinguishes `rail off`, `enabled but never connected` and `connected and healthy`. TI's own application circuit uses 10 kOhm, and the datasheet's UVLO characterisation is specified with READY = 10 k to VCC, so 10 k is the characterised value. IT IS PULLED TO THE TCA4307'S OWN VCC, ACC_3V3_SW, NOT TO +3V3 - pulling it to a permanently powered rail would push current into an unpowered device's pin and would defeat the powered-off high-impedance property that the whole isolation argument rests on. VOL 0.4 V max at 3 mA, leakage +/-1 uA, so 10 k reads as a clean logic level. IT DELIBERATELY DOES NOT CONSUME A PCAL PIN IN REV 1: it is brought out to TP44 and read with a probe. Note that while EN is low the datasheet warns current flows from VCC through the pulled-down READY pin - 0.33 mA here - but ACC_3V3_SW is OFF by default, so that costs nothing in the no-accessory state.")
			)
