		(comp
			(ref "U16")
			(value "TCA4307DGKR")
			(footprint "Package_SO:VSSOP-8_3x3mm_P0.65mm")
			(datasheet "https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tca4307.pdf")
			(description "TI TCA4307 hot-swappable I2C bus buffer with stuck-bus recovery, VSSOP-8")
			(fields
				(field
					(name "Manufacturer") "Texas Instruments")
				(field
					(name "MPN") "TCA4307DGKR")
				(field
					(name "LCSC") "C880333")
				(field
					(name "Note") "EXTERNAL I2C BUFFER - TCA9517A REPLACED BY THE TCA4307 AT FBV2-S1-009 (O-4 APPROVED). TI TCA4307DGKR, LCSC C880333, VSSOP DGK-8; verified live 2026-08-23 per D-096: 3248 in stock, $2.51 @1 / $1.71 @1k. WHY THE CHANGE: the community port is inherently HOT-PLUG and the external segment is 3.3 V ONLY, so the TCA9517A's level translation was never used while its hot-insertion and stuck-bus weaknesses were. WHAT THE TCA4307 ADDS, from SCPS270B: (1) the IN side is not connected to the OUT side until a STOP or bus-idle condition, so live insertion cannot corrupt a transfer; (2) 1 V PRECHARGE on all four SDA/SCL pins, VPRE 0.8/1/1.2 V; (3) STUCK BUS RECOVERY - SDAOUT or SCLOUT held low for tSTUCKBUS = 25 ms MIN / 40 ms typ / 65 ms MAX disconnects the bus and then issues UP TO 16 PULSES on SCLOUT at 5.5/8.5/14 kHz; (4) POWERED-OFF HIGH-IMPEDANCE I2C pins. VCC = ACC_3V3_SW, so with the accessory rail off the part is unpowered and INVISIBLE TO THE INTERNAL BUS on both sides - that is the isolation guarantee, not a firmware promise. EN = ACC_PWR_EN, active HIGH, VIH 0.7 x VCC, held LOW by `R17` 100 k on sheet 08 so the buffer is ISOLATED until firmware explicitly enables it - the safe state does not depend on the PCAL9535A reset state alone. Supports clock stretching, arbitration and synchronisation. fSCL MAX 400 kHz: THIS IS A FAST-MODE PART, NOT 1 MHz. ICC 2.5 mA typ / 4.5 mA max active, ISD 10 uA typ / 30 uA max in shutdown, UVLO 2.1 V rising. THE CIRCULAR DEPENDENCY IS BROKEN: a wedged accessory used to require the MCU to command the PCAL over the very bus that was wedged; the TCA4307 now disconnects and clocks the bus free autonomously, and ACC_PWR_EN is a second, manual lever rather than the only one. ACCESSORY COMPATIBILITY RULE: an accessory must NEVER hold SDA or SCL low for longer than 25 ms - the tSTUCKBUS MINIMUM - or the buffer will disconnect it. That forbids clock stretching beyond 25 ms and forbids slow bit-banged accessory firmware.")
				(field
					(name "Footprint") "Package_SO:VSSOP-8_3x3mm_P0.65mm")
				(field
					(name "Datasheet") "https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tca4307.pdf")
				(field
					(name "Description") "TI TCA4307 hot-swappable I2C bus buffer with stuck-bus recovery, VSSOP-8")
			)
			(libsource
				(lib "AQROOT_Beta")
				(part "TCA4307DGKR")
				(description "TI TCA4307: hot-swappable I2C bus and SMBus buffer with STUCK BUS RECOVERY. SCPS270B, Aug 2020, revised Nov 2023. VCC 2.3-5.5 V, TA -40 to 125 C, VSSOP DGK-8 (3 mm x 4.9 mm). Replaces the TCA9517A on the AQROOT community port because the port is hot-pluggable and the external segment is 3.3 V only, so level translation was never used. KEY BEHAVIOUR: (1) the IN side (SDAIN/SCLIN, the backplane) is not connected to the OUT side (SDAOUT/SCLOUT, the card) until a STOP or bus-idle condition occurs, so live insertion cannot corrupt a transfer in progress; (2) 1 V PRECHARGE on all four SDA/SCL pins (VPRE 0.8/1/1.2 V) minimises the charge dumped into the parasitic capacitance at insertion; (3) STUCK BUS RECOVERY - if SDAOUT or SCLOUT is held low for tSTUCKBUS = 25 ms MIN / 40 ms typ / 65 ms MAX the device DISCONNECTS the bus and then generates UP TO 16 PULSES on SCLOUT at 5.5/8.5/14 kHz to free the device holding the line; (4) POWERED-OFF HIGH-IMPEDANCE I2C pins, so with VCC = ACC_3V3_SW off the part is invisible to the internal bus; (5) EN is active HIGH - low puts it in shutdown, disables the rise-time accelerators and the precharge, drives READY low and isolates both sides; (6) READY is OPEN DRAIN and is high only when EN is high AND the two sides are connected. Supports clock stretching, arbitration and synchronisation. fSCL max 400 kHz - FAST MODE ONLY, NOT 1 MHz. Rise-time accelerators source 2-5 mA on a rising edge. ICC 2.5 mA typ / 4.5 mA max active, ISD 10 uA typ / 30 uA max in shutdown. UVLO 2.1 V rising, 2.0 V falling. VIH(EN) 0.7 x VCC, VIL(EN) 0.3 x VCC. CIO(SDA/SCL) 5 pF typ / 10 pF max. ACCESSORY RULE: an accessory must never hold SDA or SCL low for longer than 25 ms, the tSTUCKBUS MINIMUM, or the buffer will disconnect it.")
			)
			(property
				(name "Manufacturer")
				(value "Texas Instruments")
			)
			(property
				(name "MPN")
				(value "TCA4307DGKR")
			)
			(property
				(name "LCSC")
				(value "C880333")
			)
			(property
				(name "Note")
				(value "EXTERNAL I2C BUFFER - TCA9517A REPLACED BY THE TCA4307 AT FBV2-S1-009 (O-4 APPROVED). TI TCA4307DGKR, LCSC C880333, VSSOP DGK-8; verified live 2026-08-23 per D-096: 3248 in stock, $2.51 @1 / $1.71 @1k. WHY THE CHANGE: the community port is inherently HOT-PLUG and the external segment is 3.3 V ONLY, so the TCA9517A's level translation was never used while its hot-insertion and stuck-bus weaknesses were. WHAT THE TCA4307 ADDS, from SCPS270B: (1) the IN side is not connected to the OUT side until a STOP or bus-idle condition, so live insertion cannot corrupt a transfer; (2) 1 V PRECHARGE on all four SDA/SCL pins, VPRE 0.8/1/1.2 V; (3) STUCK BUS RECOVERY - SDAOUT or SCLOUT held low for tSTUCKBUS = 25 ms MIN / 40 ms typ / 65 ms MAX disconnects the bus and then issues UP TO 16 PULSES on SCLOUT at 5.5/8.5/14 kHz; (4) POWERED-OFF HIGH-IMPEDANCE I2C pins. VCC = ACC_3V3_SW, so with the accessory rail off the part is unpowered and INVISIBLE TO THE INTERNAL BUS on both sides - that is the isolation guarantee, not a firmware promise. EN = ACC_PWR_EN, active HIGH, VIH 0.7 x VCC, held LOW by `R17` 100 k on sheet 08 so the buffer is ISOLATED until firmware explicitly enables it - the safe state does not depend on the PCAL9535A reset state alone. Supports clock stretching, arbitration and synchronisation. fSCL MAX 400 kHz: THIS IS A FAST-MODE PART, NOT 1 MHz. ICC 2.5 mA typ / 4.5 mA max active, ISD 10 uA typ / 30 uA max in shutdown, UVLO 2.1 V rising. THE CIRCULAR DEPENDENCY IS BROKEN: a wedged accessory used to require the MCU to command the PCAL over the very bus that was wedged; the TCA4307 now disconnects and clocks the bus free autonomously, and ACC_PWR_EN is a second, manual lever rather than the only one. ACCESSORY COMPATIBILITY RULE: an accessory must NEVER hold SDA or SCL low for longer than 25 ms - the tSTUCKBUS MINIMUM - or the buffer will disconnect it. That forbids clock stretching beyond 25 ms and forbids slow bit-banged accessory firmware.")
			)
