		(libpart
			(lib "AQROOT_Beta")
			(part "DMM-4026-B-I2S")
			(description "PUI Audio bottom-port MEMS I2S microphone, 7-pad, 4.0 x 3.0 x 1.0 mm")
			(docs "https://api.puiaudio.com/filename/DMM-4026-B-I2S-R.pdf")
			(footprints
				(fp "PUI*DMM*4026*")
			)
			(fields
				(field
					(name "Reference") "MK")
				(field
					(name "Value") "DMM-4026-B-I2S")
				(field
					(name "Footprint") "AQROOT_Beta:PUI_DMM-4026-B-I2S_4.0x3.0mm")
				(field
					(name "Datasheet") "https://api.puiaudio.com/filename/DMM-4026-B-I2S-R.pdf")
				(field
					(name "Description") "PUI Audio bottom-port MEMS I2S microphone, 7-pad, 4.0 x 3.0 x 1.0 mm")
				(field
					(name "Manufacturer") "PUI Audio")
				(field
					(name "MPN") "DMM-4026-B-I2S-R")
				(field
					(name "Package") "PUI 7-pad SMD, 4.00 x 3.00 x 1.00 mm, bottom acoustic port")
				(field
					(name "Note") "Verified against the PUI Audio DMM-4026-B-I2S-R data sheet (Rev A, 5/26/2021) in FBV2-S1-006. SEVEN pads, not six - it is not pin-compatible with the ICS-43434 it replaces. Pin 1 LR: low selects the LEFT I2S slot, high selects RIGHT. Pin 2 CONFIG: Bosch-style config strap - the data sheet says: Pull to ground. The state of this pin is used at power-up. It MUST be tied to GND. The ICS-43434 has no equivalent pin. Pin 3 VDD 1.62 to 3.63 V, decouple with 0.1 uF. Pin 4 GND is the ring pad around the acoustic port. Pin 7 SD tri-states when it is not driving its own channel, and the data sheet requires a 100 kOhm pull-down on the SD trace to discharge the line while all microphones on the bus are tri-stated. Normal-mode input clock 2.048 to 4.096 MHz; below 320 kHz the part enters sleep mode at 5 uA. Data is I2S 24-bit in a 32-bit word (mono) or 64-bit frame (stereo), 18-bit precision, six null bits. Supply current 820 to 1000 uA normal. Startup 20 ms. Sensitivity -26 dBFS, SNR 64 dB, omnidirectional. Bottom port, acoustic port diameter 0.25 mm in the can; the PCB needs a 1.05 mm hole concentric with pad 4.")
			)
