				(field
					(name "Description") "Low-voltage 16-bit I2C-bus I/O port with interrupt and Agile I/O, TSSOP-24; pin-to-pin replacement for PCA9535/PCA9535A/TCA9535")
				(field
					(name "Manufacturer") "NXP Semiconductors")
				(field
					(name "MPN") "PCAL9535APW,118")
				(field
					(name "Note") "AQROOT FBV2-S1-008. NXP data sheet Rev. 2, 23 January 2015 (SOT355-1, TSSOP24, body width 4.4 mm). VDD 1.65-5.5 V, 5 V-tolerant I/O, 400 kHz Fast-mode. Slave address 0 1 0 0 A2 A1 A0 -> 0x20 with A0=A1=A2=GND. Outputs sink 25 mA for direct LED drive (abs max 50 mA continuous per I/O, 200 mA total ISS, 200 mW Ptot). POWER-UP STATE, FROM THE COMMAND-BYTE TABLE: Configuration 06h/07h = FFh so every pin is a high-impedance INPUT; Output port 02h/03h = FFh so a pin drives HIGH the instant it is made an output; pull-up/pull-down ENABLE 46h/47h = 00h so the internal 100 k resistors are DISABLED; Interrupt mask 4Ah/4Bh = FFh so ALL interrupts are masked. P-port input leakage IIH/IIL <= 1 uA. AGILE I/O over the TCA9535: programmable 100 k pull-up/pull-down, interrupt mask, interrupt STATUS registers 4Ch/4Dh that identify the changed input, input latch, and four output drive strengths.")
			)
